WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.575
Now the second half of the rule, and this one is for every vessel, radar or not.

2
00:00:05.825 --> 00:00:07.675
It’s about what you hear.

3
00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:12.750
Suppose you hear a fog signal, and it seems to come from forward of your beam.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.225
Or suppose you simply can’t avoid a close-quarters situation with a vessel forward of your beam.

5
00:00:19.475 --> 00:00:24.125
Then you shall reduce your speed to the minimum at which you can keep your course.

6
00:00:24.375 --> 00:00:26.125
Bare steerageway.

7
00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:29.275
If necessary, you take all your way off.

8
00:00:29.525 --> 00:00:31.025
You stop.

9
00:00:31.275 --> 00:00:37.325
And in any event, you navigate with extreme caution until the danger of collision is over.

10
00:00:37.575 --> 00:00:43.300
The only exception is when you’ve already determined that no risk of collision exists.

11
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:47.825
Notice one small word in the rule: apparently.

12
00:00:48.075 --> 00:00:51.175
The signal is apparently forward of your beam.

13
00:00:51.425 --> 00:00:53.450
Why would the rule say that?

14
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.200
Because sound plays tricks in fog.

15
00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:01.000
It bends, it echoes, and it can seem to come from the wrong direction.

16
00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.900
So when you hear a horn ahead, don’t guess, and don’t turn.

17
00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:07.025
Slow down first.
